    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213-a1">

                <pb facs="0395" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg295"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    594.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fouchard to Mr.
                            Langston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1883-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 13, 1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In the interest of humanity I have
                    the honor to transmit to you under this cover the address of this day of his
                    excellency the President of Hayti to the rebels of the cities of Jacmel and of
                    Jérémie. You will perhaps judge it necessary <pb facs="0396" n="296"
                        xml:id="pg296"/> to do that which shall be in your power to save the
                    innocent and neutrals who are in Jérémie and Jacmel exposed to the misfortunes
                    which menace these cities, if, in the delay fixed, they do not submit themselves
                    to the constitutional government.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. FOUCHARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
